# Ask as an add-on for an existing Chiron. Copy to .env and fill in; then:
#   docker compose up -d --build        (the Ask container)
#   add the /ask route to the web server   (proxy/)
#   turn the tab on in the UI               (README.md, "The Ask tab")
#   python3 check.py
# Paths are on this machine. Secrets stay in this file: keep it mode 600 and out of git.

# docker compose reads this file too. The COMPOSE_FILE lines below list files with ":",
# and this keeps ":" working on Windows as well.
COMPOSE_PATH_SEPARATOR=:

# --- the Chiron this Ask is added to --------------------------------------------------
# The Chiron checkout: the directory holding chiron/ and requirements/. The image is
# built from it, so Ask runs the deployment's own Chiron code.
CHIRON_SRC=/srv/chiron/is4r-chiron
# The Django project (the directory holding manage.py), mounted read-only: its settings
# module and custom processors are what Ask runs with. CHIRON_SETTINGS names the settings
# module if it is not project.settings.
CHIRON_PROJECT_DIR=/srv/chiron/is4r-chiron/test_project
#CHIRON_SETTINGS=project.settings

# The two databases, as the CONTAINER reaches them: a Postgres on this machine is
# host.docker.internal, not localhost. The metadata database must be Postgres (SQLite
# file locks do not cross the container boundary); the warehouse is whatever
# CHIRON_SQL_ALCHEMY_CONNECTION_STRING says, written for the container.
CHIRON_MCP_METADATA_DB=postgresql://chiron:secret@host.docker.internal:5432/chiron_meta
CHIRON_MCP_WAREHOUSE_URL=postgresql://chiron:secret@host.docker.internal:5432/chiron
# A Chiron in Docker on this machine whose database port is not published: its Docker
# network (docker network ls), and compose.network.yml turned on with COMPOSE_FILE. The
# two URLs above then name the database's service (db:5432), not host.docker.internal.
#CHIRON_NETWORK=
#COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yml:compose.network.yml

# --- the site -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where people open Chiron, with the path prefix if it has one (https://example.org/chiron).
# The web server serves /ask on this same address, which is how Ask knows who is logged in.
PUBLIC_URL=https://chiron.example.org
# The port (and address) the web server forwards /ask to. This machine only by default.
#ASK_BIND=127.0.0.1:8900
# A Chiron on this computer with no web server in front (Django's dev server, or Chiron
# in Docker): the address browsers use to open Ask directly, the same as the UI's
# VITE_ASK_URL. Leave it unset behind a web server, where Ask is PUBLIC_URL/ask.
#ASK_URL=http://localhost:8900

# --- what Ask may see -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The access ceiling: whatever the logged-in person has in Chiron, capped here
# (agg, deid or phi). Questions and their figures go to the model's provider.
CHIRON_MCP_MAX_ACCESS_LEVEL=deid
# Conversations (their transcripts and traces) are kept for good; a number here is the
# idle hours after which they are deleted instead.
#CHIRON_MCP_THREAD_TTL_HOURS=0
#CHIRON_MCP_TURN_SECONDS=240
# A Django group whose members see everyone's usage and who has what access at
# /ask/usage, as superusers do (anyone else sees their own usage there).
#CHIRON_MCP_USAGE_GROUP=ask-admins

# --- the models -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Patient data: to answer, Ask sends the question and what it reads from Chiron (patient
# rows too, when the person may see them) to the model. If a dataset holds PHI, use only a
# model service your organization has approved for PHI (covered by a business associate
# agreement, a BAA), or a model on your own computer or network. Never a personal account.
#
# The models people may switch between, as id=Label pairs separated by commas (Haiku is
# the default when listed, else Opus, else the first). Unset: one model, no menu.
#CHIRON_MCP_ASK_MODELS=claude-haiku-5-5=Haiku 5.5,claude-sonnet-5-5=Sonnet 5.5
#
# Which model answers: set ONE of these.
#  * Claude, with an Anthropic API key:
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#  * Claude on Amazon Bedrock: these lines, and credentials from the machine's role (on
#    EC2) or from an AWS profile (compose.aws.yml). Bedrock's ids start with us.anthropic.
#CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK=1
#AWS_REGION=us-east-1
#AWS_PROFILE=
#ANTHROPIC_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5
#  * OpenAI or Google Gemini, through LiteLLM: keep the models you want in litellm.yaml,
#    turn LiteLLM on with COMPOSE_FILE, and set the keys. LITELLM_MASTER_KEY is any long
#    random string, such as: python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(24))"
#COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yml:compose.litellm.yml
#OPENAI_API_KEY=
#GEMINI_API_KEY=
#LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=
#CHIRON_MCP_ASK_MODELS=gpt-6.2-sol=GPT-6.2 Sol,gemini-3.8-flash=Gemini 3.8 Flash
#  * a model on your own computer or network: Ollama speaks Ask's format itself. On this
#    machine it is host.docker.internal (on Linux, start Ollama with OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0).
#    Name its model in CHIRON_MCP_ASK_MODELS so every model slot uses it; it needs good
#    tool calling and a context of 64k tokens or more. Other servers (vLLM, LM Studio)
#    go through LiteLLM, as an entry in litellm.yaml.
#ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
#ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=not-needed
#DISABLE_PROMPT_CACHING=1
#CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_BETAS=1
#CHIRON_MCP_ASK_MODELS=your-model=Your model
#  * a Claude account (Pro or Max), only to try Ask yourself: leave all of the above
#    unset and log the container in once: docker compose exec -it ask claude
# Claude Code's own extras, off in a server
DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1
CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1

# --- build ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION=2.1.283
# 0 lets the deployment's own version pins win over chiron-mcp's constraints.txt
#USE_CONSTRAINTS=1
# How often Postgres checks that Ask still waits for a query, in ms. 0 (the default) works
# with every Postgres, one installed directly on a Mac or Windows PC too. A Postgres on
# Linux can take 2000, so that it stops a query whose answer was cancelled.
#CHIRON_MCP_PG_CHECK_INTERVAL=2000

# --- a proxy, when the network reaches the internet through one ------------------------
# (for building, set the proxy in Docker Desktop: Settings, Resources, Proxies)
#HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example.org:8080
#NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1,host.docker.internal,litellm

# --- check.py -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# a Chiron account with access to a dataset, for the end-to-end check (no password: the
# check makes a session inside the container)
#ASK_CHECK_USER=demouser
#ASK_CHECK_DATASET=
